WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.550
Now that the year's horror releases are all
but set in stone, film studios are looking

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.950
ahead to draw audiences to theaters with a
brand new round of exciting trailers.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.360
What treats did September deliver?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.900
Here's a roundup of all the best trailers
from September 2018.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.440
First Man

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.520
Apollo 11 may have put a man on the moon,
but First Man is putting the humanity in the

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.020
moon landing.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.540
The latest trailer for Universal's dramatic
biopic about Neil Armstrong plays out under

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:30.420
stock audio of JFK's "moon speech," as Ryan
Gosling's Armstrong contemplates everything

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.730
he's about to leave behind.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.860
It's a pretty moving trailer, and it serves
as the perfect last-minute hype-builder for

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.420
a movie that's already seeing an overwhelmingly
positive response from early screenings.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.100
Get ready for the ride of your life when First
Man touches down October 12th.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.700
Hunter Killer

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:50.860
Gary Oldman is a true chameleon, one of those
actors who can transition seamlessly from

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.340
an Oscar-winning portrayal of Winston Churchill
to being the voice of a house in a silly Netflix

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:55.840
movie.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.260
"The walls are treated with a layer of smartpaint and
reinforced with nano materials.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:00.760
Hun?

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.780
The walls are treated with a layer of smartpaint and
reinforced with okay, I got it."

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.540
What will he bring to Lionsgate's submarine
action thriller Hunter Killer?

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.100
Only God knows.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.800
The plot of the movie follows Gerard Butler's
Captain Glass, a submarine commander who's

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.390
on a mission to rescue the president of Russia.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.840
How many bad guys are they going to have to
fight through to get him back?

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.520
Gary Oldman knows!

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.760
"Everyone!"

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.170
The trailer is heavy on the torpedoes and
light on anything else, but Hunter Killer

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.760
looks like a fun action-packed blockbuster.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:32.840
Take a look on October 26th.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.480
The Girl in the Spider's Web

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:39.380
Each new trailer for The Girl in the Spider's
Web unravels that web a little more, offering

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.780
up new plot details and tantalizing glimpses
of the action to come.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.100
The film is an adaptation of the fourth book
in the Millennium series, which sees Lisbeth

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.490
Salander on the run from the NSA after hacking
into their servers.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.720
She'll have to team up with her old buddy
Mikael Blomkvist to sort out a brand new conspiracy.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.800
The trailer also reveals that Salander will
have a run-in with her estranged sister.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.920
Expect plenty of snow, leather, and hacking
when The Girl in the Spider's Web spins into

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.260
theaters on November 9th.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.820
The Ballad of Buster Scruggs

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.080
When it was first announced, The Ballad of
Buster Scruggs was supposed to be the first

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.820
TV series written and developed by the Coen
brothers.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:19.160
It's since been changed to an anthology film,
but the underlying premise remains the same:

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.920
it's an offbeat comedy Western that was pieced
together over the past 25 years from scraps

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.180
of stories that the brothers just had no idea
what else to do with.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.980
That may sound a little absurd, but if anyone
can pull it off it's Joel and Ethan Coen,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.530
the duo behind similarly absurd cult classics
such as O Brother, Where Art Thou? and Raising

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:37.020
Arizona.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.800
"Son, you got a panty on your head."

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.200
Look for The Ballad of Buster Scruggs on Netflix
and in select theaters on November 16th.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.320
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.260
In The Crimes of Grindelwald, Newt Scamander
is back on a brand new quest at the behest

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.880
of Albus Dumbledore - the villainous Grindelwald
has magically escaped from magic prison, and

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.740
Dumbledore needs Newt to bring him back in…
with magic!

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.580
Johnny Depp stars as Grindelwald, who's using
his free time to recruit an army of followers

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.860
to help him rule the world.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.060
Great Gellert!

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.420
The stakes have never been higher, and you
can watch it all unfold when Fantastic Beasts:

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.520
The Crimes of Grindelwald apparates into theaters
on November 16th.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.020
Creed II

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.870
The Rocky franchise has always been less about
boxing and more about breaking the audience's

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.420
hearts in between slick training montages,
and it looks like we're going to get a double

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.140
dose of both with Creed II.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:36.480
This time, Adonis will be squaring off against
Viktor Drago, the son of Ivan Drago, who killed

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.300
Apollo Creed in Rocky IV.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:42.900
Now, the next generation of fans gets to watch
the next generation of big-screen boxers duke

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.240
it out for the heavyweight title.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.360
Michael B. Jordan, Tessa Thompson, and ol'
Sly Stallone are returning to their roles

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:53.340
from the first Creed, with a special appearance
by Dolph Lundgren as the Siberian Bull himself,

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.180
Ivan Drago.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.700
Step into the ring on November 21st.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.240
Mary Poppins Returns

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.700
The original Mary Poppins is a childhood classic,
a magical romp through the imagination led

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.940
by Julie Andrews.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.760
2018's Mary Poppins Returns won't be a remake,
but a direct sequel to the 1964 original.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:15.320
A new tragedy summons Mary Poppins back into
the lives of the Banks kids from the original,

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.440
who are now adults.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.470
They'll all set off on a new adventure that
teaches these grumpy grown-ups that getting

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.840
older doesn't necessarily mean you have to
lose your sense of childhood wonder.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:28.900
Ben Whishaw and Emily Mortimer play the adult
Michael and Jane Banks, and the ageless Mary

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.740
Poppins will be played by Emily Blunt.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.100
Look for it on December 19, just in time for
Christmas.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.640
Holmes and Watson

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.920
After months of hearing about the upcoming
Will Ferrell and John C. Reilly team-up comedy

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.760
Holmes and Watson, expectations were pretty
high.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.740
This was supposed to be Step Brothers, but
with mysteries.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.400
"What are you doing?"

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.240
I'm burying you.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:49.540
I'm alive!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.000
I'm alive.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.600
Shh waking the neighbors, shut up."

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.580
Instead of all that, the trailer for Holmes
and Watson just gives us two and a half minutes

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.780
of vaguely comedic… stuff.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.150
To be fair, this is just the trailer.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.080
It could get better.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:12.280
Comedies are particularly hard to market,
so there's still hope for Holmes and Watson

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.630
to turn out to be legitimately funny.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:18.050
We'll be able to finally solve this mystery
when Holmes and Watson hits theaters on December

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:18.700
21st.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:19.660
Bumblebee

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.380
Cars and trucks are cool, sure - but do you
know what's cooler?

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.220
Cars and trucks with feelings.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:30.200
As the Transformers franchise's first prequel,
Bumblebee is shifting gears for a more down-to-earth

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:34.210
experience that looks like a far cry from
the city-smashing extravaganzas offered by

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.229
the main run of Transformers films.

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:37.300
Y'know, stuff like this:

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.940
In the newest trailer, Bumblebee deepens his

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.860
emotional bond with young Charlie as they're
both caught up in a war that's beyond their

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.360
control.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.040
It's like Herbie: Reloaded, if Herbie was
reloaded with actual bullets.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.760
Look for Bumblebee in theaters on December
21st.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.220
Dark Phoenix

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:02.400
20th Century Fox has gone down the Dark Phoenix
road once before, and it turned out to be

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.040
a very dark road indeed.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:10.000
2006's X-Men: The Last Stand marked a notoriously
troubled end to the original X-Men cinematic

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.340
trilogy, and it made a mess of one of the
most beloved character arcs in X-Men comics

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.460
history: The Dark Phoenix Saga.

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:21.130
Based on the trailer for Dark Phoenix, it
looks like the story may finally get the live-action

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.320
adaptation it deserves.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.780
Throughout the trailer, we see Jean slowly
turning to the dark side after absorbing the

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.200
Phoenix Force during a freak solar flare accident
in space.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.380
It seems to hit all the right notes, and you
can look for Dark Phoenix to hit theaters

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.880
on June 7, 2019

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.240
Captive State

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.740
From Rupert Wyatt, director of Rise of the
Planet of the Apes, Captive State is an upcoming

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:47.900
sci-fi thriller about a world that's been
occupied by an extraterrestrial force.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:53.640
In exchange for peace and prosperity for all
mankind, the aliens only want one thing: total

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.500
domination.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.260
Those darn aliens!

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:00.420
"Peace among worlds, Rick."

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.300
The teaser trailer for Captive State shows
a ton of promise, focusing mainly on the film's

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.430
hellish dystopian imagery while a voiceover
repeats the words "Give thanks."

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:13.960
Moonlight's Ashton Sanders stars alongside
John Goodman and Vera Farmiga, and Captive

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.720
State is slated for a March 2019 release.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.480
Captain Marvel

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:23.479
Ever since that end-credits scene of Avengers:
Infinity War, fans have been clamoring for

00:07:23.479 --> 00:07:26.229
more glimpses of Brie Larson as Captain Marvel.

00:07:26.229 --> 00:07:29.440
Now, we finally got our wish in the form of
a full-length trailer.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:30.560
Was the wait worth it?

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:31.740
Yeah, kind of!

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.980
Brie Larson does plenty of Captain Marvely
things in the trailer, like jumping around,

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:36.880
and being powerful.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.100
What else happens?

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.180
Glad you asked!

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.660
First, she crash lands in a Blockbuster video
store, because this movie takes place in that

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:46.380
distant part of the past known as the 1990s.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.740
Even Captain Marvel can't figure out what
that place is.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:51.960
She's so out of touch with the world that
she punches someone's grandma.

00:07:51.979 --> 00:07:53.960
What'd you think she was, Carol?

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:54.460
A Skrull?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:58.580
This trailer does build a lot of expectations
for the movie, and we honestly can't wait

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.860
to see it when Captain Marvel hits theaters
on March 8th, 2019.

